Z||000001||Old Lar||10-24-2001||07:07 PM||||Code 32 is a bit*h to get rid of.  Iv'e had it on my 87 GT for 3 years, probably some small vacuum leak.  Engine light comes on while driving intermittantly, but goes away once the car is shut off, then turned back on.  It hasn't seemed to affect the cars performance.<P>Code 24: TPS setting, connection at ECM. Haynes Manual<P>Code 44: ECM wire connections terminals 15 and 8. Vacuum leak at the TBI base gasket, vacuum hoses or the intake manfold gasket.  Replace O2 sensor. Haynes Manual<P>Looks like vacuum leaks or ECM connections are the common line.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
