Z||000004||87GTZ34||10-25-2001||06:05 PM||||If the EGR is actually in good working order, usually the code 32 means that the electrical 'check switch' is having problems.   If EGR doesn't work with a good EGR valve, then the actuator valve needs to be replaced.  Both the actuator switch and the check switch are integrated into a single unit.  Right now I've bypassed my actuator (from vacuum) and I only intermittantly get the check engine light to come on.  This is because the 'check switch' isn't working correctly.||||reg||1
